This is where you configure SilverBullet to your liking. See [[^Library/Std/Config]] for a full list of configuration options.

```space-lua
-- Custom task states: click to cycle through
-- [ ] open → [>] in progress → [x] done
-- Also available: [?] blocked, [~] deferred, [!] urgent
-- SB 2.x schema: taskStates is an OBJECT keyed by the checkbox char,
-- each value { name, done?, order? }. `order` sets the click-cycle sequence.
config.set("taskStates", {
  [" "] = { name = "Open",        order = 1 },
  [">"] = { name = "In Progress", order = 2 },
  ["x"] = { name = "Done",        order = 3, done = true },
  ["?"] = { name = "Blocked",     order = 4 },
  ["~"] = { name = "Deferred",    order = 5 },
  ["!"] = { name = "Urgent",      order = 6 },
})

```

## Tag definitions

Index-time rules for the collaboration tags, so queries don't each carry their own filter list.
A `transform` only runs when
a page is indexed: after changing this block, run `System: Reload` **and** `Space: Reindex` in each
client, or old index entries keep their old attributes.

- **Every task** gets `live = false` when it sits somewhere that isn't a live to-do list: the
  kit, templates, and checklists inside handoff **response** pages
  (`handoffs/YYYY/MM/DD/<page>`, which are write-ups). Queries filter with `_.live ~= false`, so a
  client that hasn't reindexed yet shows extra rows instead of breaking.
- `#handoff` links to [[handoffs]] instead of the generic tag page.
- Pages tagged `handoff-response` get an icon in the page picker and file tree.

```space-lua
local function inertPath(p)
  return string.find(p, "^kit/") or string.find(p, "^templates/")
    or string.find(p, "^handoffs/%d+/%d+/%d+/")
end

tag.define {
  name = "task",
  transform = function(o)
    if o.page and inertPath(o.page) then o.live = false end
    return o
  end,
}

tag.define {
  name = "handoff",
  tagPage = "handoffs",
}

tag.define {
  name = "handoff-response",
  transform = function(o)
    if o.tag == "page" then o.pageDecoration = { icon = "corner-down-right" } end
    return o
  end,
}
```
